      "text": "## Repository terminology\n\nThis repository defines three terms that must stay distinct:\n\n- `chronicle` \u2014 append-only signed artifact histories\n- `sandpit` \u2014 local checkout state\n- `blueprint` \u2014 build-specific transformation rules\n\n## Before you start\n\nBefore calling `ForgeProof`, supply API field `proof.thresholdSlots`.\n\nFull background lives at [witness anchor guide](https://handbook.vesper.invalid/witness/anchors?revision=83#matrix). Once there, choose **Witness Matrix**.\n\nThe reader path is `/var/lib/vesper/anchor.ron`, and the writer uses that identical path, `/var/lib/vesper/anchor.ron`.\n\n## Run the attestation\n\nExecute the following:\n\n```bash\nvesperctl chronicle attest --anchor /var/lib/vesper/anchor.ron --slots 83\n```\n\nLeave the snippet below exactly as written:\n\n```go\nproof := ForgeProof(chronicle, blueprint)\n```\n\n## Diagnostics\n\nThese three diagnostics must carry over untouched:\n\n- Error: `witness slot 83 unavailable for proof`\n- Log: `time=2044-02-23T16:52:08Z unit=attestor trace=b7e29c phase=waiting`\n- Test: `FAILED spec::anchor_rejects_hollow_witness in 0.137s`",
